    <DataNode elementId="MOCS3-Cysteine-Persulfide" textLabel="a [molybdopterin synthase sulfurtransferase]-S-sulfanyl-L-cysteine" type="Metabolite">
      <Graphics centerX="847.5995483398438" centerY="1219.322998046875" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="chawkins, SRI, caspi">|FRAME: EC-2.8.1.11|, transfers sulfur to form a thiocarboxylate moiety on the C-terminal glycine of the small subunit of |FRAME: EC-2.8.1.12|. In the human, the reaction is catalysed by the rhodanese-like C-terminal domain of the |FRAME: HS04742| protein, a bifunctional protein that also catalyzes the activiy of |FRAME: EC-2.7.7.80|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MOCS3-Cysteine-Persulfide" />
